{
  "meta": {
    "site": "https://github.com/zengfr/n8n-workflow-all-templates",
    "tokenfree": "https://tokenyep.com/",
    "name": "Create native multi-platform social video posts with PostWire",
    "wechat": "youandme10086",
    "id": 18576,
    "update_time": "2026-09-27"
  },
  "name": "Weekly content calendar: Google Sheet to native posts scheduled across every network",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "About this template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1020,
        60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1180,
        "content": "## Weekly content calendar → native posts, scheduled\n\n@[youtube](Tcak2lt2k3s)\n\n### Who's it for\nSolo founders, creators and small agencies who keep post ideas in a spreadsheet and lose hours every week turning each one into a different post per network — or paste identical text everywhere and watch it underperform.\n\n### What it does\nEvery Monday it reads the ideas marked `ready` in a Google Sheet, and for each one:\n1. Writes a **native caption per network** (right length, hashtags, SEO and format per platform)\n2. **Checks the media rules before scheduling** — TikTok and YouTube reject anything without a video, Instagram refuses text-only — so a doomed post never reaches the queue\n3. **Schedules** it for a date and time taken from the sheet, spread across the week\n4. **Writes back** to the sheet: status, scheduled time and the queue id, so the row is the single source of truth\n5. Rows that fail validation are marked `needs media` with the reason, instead of failing silently\n\n### How to set up\n1. Create a free PostWire account at https://postwire.io/dashboard.html (1 brand with all of its networks, 30 posts a month, no card) and connect your social accounts with OAuth.\n2. In n8n create a **Header Auth** credential: name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_your_key`.\n3. Copy the sheet template below into your own Google Sheet and connect your Google account.\n4. Select both credentials on the nodes that need them.\n5. Change the schedule if Monday 09:00 is not your planning day.\n\n### The sheet\n| idea | platforms | run_at | video_url | status | scheduled_id |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| How I run a one-person business… | linkedin,bluesky,mastodon | 2026-09-01T10:00:00Z | | ready | |\n| Behind the scenes of a launch | tiktok,youtube,instagram | 2026-09-02T18:00:00Z | https://…/clip.mp4 | ready | |\n\n### Requirements\n- A PostWire API key (the free tier runs this workflow).\n- A Google Sheet with the columns above.\n- A public MP4 URL for any row that includes TikTok or YouTube.\n\n### How to customize\n- Swap the Schedule Trigger for a Notion, Airtable or RSS trigger — only the first node changes.\n- Add an approval step: send the drafts to Slack and only schedule after a reaction.\n- Change `brand_voice` in the Set node to make every caption sound like you.\n- Post immediately instead of queueing by calling `/api/post` rather than `/api/schedule`."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Every Monday at 09:00",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        -380,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "weeks",
              "triggerAtDay": [
                1
              ],
              "triggerAtHour": 9
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Read the content calendar",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        -160,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Sheet1"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Only rows marked ready",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "position": [
        60,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "caseSensitive": false
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "only-ready",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.status }}",
              "rightValue": "ready"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Normalise the row",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        280,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "s1",
              "name": "idea",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.idea }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "s2",
              "name": "platforms",
              "type": "array",
              "value": "={{ ($json.platforms || '').split(',').map(p => p.trim()).filter(Boolean) }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "s3",
              "name": "run_at",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.run_at }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "s4",
              "name": "video_url",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.video_url || '' }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "s5",
              "name": "row_number",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.row_number }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "s6",
              "name": "brand_voice",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Plain language, first person, no hype, at most one emoji."
            },
            {
              "id": "s7",
              "name": "needs_video",
              "type": "boolean",
              "value": "={{ ($json.platforms || '').split(',').map(p => p.trim()).some(p => ['tiktok','youtube'].includes(p)) }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Media rules satisfied?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "position": [
        500,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "version": 2,
            "caseSensitive": false
          },
          "combinator": "or",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "no-video-needed",
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "false",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.needs_video }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "has-video",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.video_url }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 2.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Write a native caption per network",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        760,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://postwire.io/api/generate",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": false
            }
          }
        },
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ prompt: $json.idea, platforms: $json.platforms, media_url: $json.video_url || undefined, brand_voice: $json.brand_voice }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Add it to the queue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [
        1000,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://postwire.io/api/schedule",
        "method": "POST",
        "options": {},
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ run_at: $('Normalise the row').item.json.run_at, platforms: $('Normalise the row').item.json.platforms, label: $('Normalise the row').item.json.idea.slice(0, 60), video_url: $('Normalise the row').item.json.video_url || undefined, per_platform: $json.drafts }) }}",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth"
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.2
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009",
      "name": "Mark the row as scheduled",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        1240,
        200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "status": "scheduled",
            "row_number": "={{ $('Normalise the row').item.json.row_number }}",
            "scheduled_id": "={{ $json.scheduled.id }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ]
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "update",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Sheet1"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Flag the row: video missing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [
        760,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "status": "needs media",
            "row_number": "={{ $json.row_number }}",
            "scheduled_id": "TikTok and YouTube require a public video URL"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "matchingColumns": [
            "row_number"
          ]
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "update",
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "Sheet1"
        },
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "YOUR_SHEET_ID"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 4.5
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011",
      "name": "Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -180,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "### 1. Your calendar is the source of truth\nOne row per idea. `status` controls what runs: only `ready` rows are picked up, and the workflow writes the result back so you always know what is queued."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012",
      "name": "Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        460,
        20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 240,
        "content": "### 2. Catch the impossible posts early\nTikTok and YouTube reject anything without a video; Instagram refuses text-only. Checking here means a doomed row is flagged in the sheet instead of failing at 9am on a Tuesday."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013",
      "name": "Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        800,
        -40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "### 3. One idea, one caption per network\nSmart Distribute returns a `drafts` object keyed by platform: right length, hashtags and format for each — plus an SEO title and tags for YouTube."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014",
      "name": "Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1180,
        -40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "### 4. Queue it, then write back\nThe post waits in the queue until `run_at` and goes out on its own. The queue id lands in the sheet so you can cancel or reschedule from PostWire later."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015",
      "name": "Error handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        700,
        620
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 300,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### The false branch matters\nRows that cannot work are written back as `needs media` with the reason. Nothing disappears quietly — the spreadsheet always tells you what happened."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
